  "id": "18496",
  "key": "SFCC-257",
  "summary": "Spike: Playwright Spec Generation from Zephyr Test Cases",
  "description": "## Objective\n\nInvestigate and document how a Dev/Tester generates Playwright spec files from Zephyr test cases — so the squad has a confirmed, repeatable pattern for converting documented test cases into executable automation scripts.\n\n## Background\n\nZephyr test cases define what to test; Playwright specs define how to automate it. The gap between the two is currently manual and inconsistent. This spike confirms the workflow: who generates the spec, what inputs they use from Zephyr, how the spec is structured, and where it lives in the repository.\n\n## Tasks\n\n- Confirm the source format: what fields from a Zephyr test case map to a Playwright spec (test name, steps, assertions, data)\n- Define who is responsible for spec generation — Dev, Tester, or shared — and when in the sprint cycle this happens\n- Document the spec file structure and naming convention to be used across the project\n- Confirm where Playwright specs are stored in the repository and how they are linked back to Zephyr test cases\n- Identify any tooling or templates that accelerate spec generation from Zephyr\n\n## Definition of Done\n\nA documented pattern confirming how Playwright specs are generated from Zephyr test cases, including ownership, file structure, naming convention, repository location, and a worked example — with Technical Lead sign-off and sufficient detail for any Dev or Tester on the squad to follow.",
