  "description": "## Objective\nInvestigate and document how Playwright specs are executed automatically via BrowserStack across all 8 storefronts and the defined browser/device matrix — so the squad has a confirmed, repeatable pipeline for cross-storefront automated test execution.\n## Background\nThe Zimmermann project covers 8 storefronts, each requiring validation across a browser and device matrix. Running these manually is not scalable. This spike confirms the BrowserStack integration with Playwright, the configuration required per storefront, the browser/device matrix to be used, and how results are reported back to the team.\n## Tasks\n- Confirm BrowserStack account access, project setup, and authentication model for the SFCC project\n- Define the browser and device matrix to be used across the 8 storefronts\n- Document the Playwright  BrowserStack configuration (capabilities, parallelisation, environment variables, storefront-specific config)\n- Confirm how test runs are triggered — manual, CI/CD pipeline, or scheduled — and the integration with GitHub Actions or equivalent\n- Document how results are reported: BrowserStack dashboard, Zephyr update, or Jira comment\n- Identify any storefront-specific differences that affect how the matrix is applied\n## Definition of Done\nA documented pattern confirming the BrowserStack  Playwright execution setup for all 8 storefronts and the browser/device matrix, including trigger mechanism, configuration approach, and results reporting — with Technical Lead sign-off and sufficient detail for the squad to execute and maintain the pipeline.",
