{"result":"{
  "id": "17828",
  "key": "SFCC-2",
  "summary": "PWA Kit Components",
  "description": "**Epic Summary**\n\nBuild and maintain the shared UI component library for the Zimmermann PWA Kit storefront. This covers foundational design system elements — typography, icons, logo, colour tokens, and reusable UI components — that are consumed across all frontend epics.\n\n**Business Value / Objective**\n\nA consistent, well-documented component library ensures visual consistency across all 8 storefronts and speeds up frontend development by giving Squad B a shared set of building blocks to work from rather than rebuilding common elements per page.\n\n**Scope**\n\nIn Scope:\n\n- UI component library setup (typography, icons, logo, colour tokens)\n- Reusable PWA Kit components consumed across frontend epics\n\nOut of Scope:\n\n- Motion design guidelines and animation behaviour — covered in Motion Design (SFCC-86)\n- Page-level layout and feature build — covered in their respective epics (PDP, PLP, Homepage, etc.)\n- SFCC Business Manager configuration — covered in Platform Setup (SFCC-1)\n\n**Dependencies**\n\n- SFCC-1 (Platform Setup & Environments) — PWA Kit scaffold must be in place\n- Figma design assets and design handoff from Zimmermann design team\n\n**Assumptions & Constraints**\n\n- Component library serves all 8 storefronts with regional variations handled at the page/epic level\n- Zimmermann design team provides Figma files as the source of truth for component specs",
