{"result":"{
  "id": "18495",
  "key": "SFCC-256",
  "summary": "Spike: Zephyr Test Case Creation via MCP from Approved User Story ACs",
  "description": "## Objective\n\nInvestigate and document how MCP can be used to automatically generate Zephyr test cases from the approved Acceptance Criteria of each User Story — so the squad has a confirmed, repeatable pattern for test case creation ahead of QA execution.\n\n## Background\n\nManually creating Zephyr test cases from story ACs is time-consuming and inconsistent across the team. MCP offers a potential mechanism to automate this step. This spike confirms whether the integration is viable, what the trigger and input shape looks like, and what the output test case structure in Zephyr should be.\n\n## Tasks\n\n- Confirm MCP's access to Jira and Zephyr and the authentication/permission model required\n- Map the input: identify which AC fields from a User Story MCP reads and how they are structured\n- Map the output: define what a generated Zephyr test case should contain (test name, steps, expected result, linked story)\n- Document the confirmed pattern with an example end-to-end run against a sample story\n- Identify any limitations or manual review steps required before test cases are approved for use\n\n## Definition of Done\n\nA documented pattern (TSD or findings document) confirming how MCP generates Zephyr test cases from approved story ACs, with a worked example and Technical Lead sign-off — sufficient for the squad to apply the pattern consistently across all stories.",
  "status": {
    "name": "Done",
    "category": "Done",
    "color": "green"
  },
